<header><p class="enc-kicker">Term · currency</p><h1 class="enc-title">Biatec</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Biatec is a name, probably that of a Celtic ruler, inscribed on large <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> coins minted in the 1st century BCE at the oppidum on the site of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bratislava">Bratislava</a>, in the lands of the Boii. The coins are among the most important Celtic finds in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, and the Biatec design was used on the Slovak five-crown coin.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/biatec.jpg" alt="Biatec" width="320" height="158" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: matissek · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Web_Biatec.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
